  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the traced flow:\n\n1. **FastAPI body param solving**: `fastapi/routing.py` (`get_request_handler`) reads and JSON-decodes the request body, then calls `solve_dependencies()` in `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py`, which calls `request_body_to_args()` \u2192 `field.validate(value, ...)`.\n2. **Pydantic v2 boundary**: `ModelField.validate()` in `fastapi/_compat.py` calls `self._type_adapter.validate_python(value, from_attributes=True)` \u2014 a `TypeAdapter` built over the field's annotation + `FieldInfo`, i.e. it invokes pydantic-core's compiled validator for the body model.\n3. **Schema construction**: `pydantic/_internal/_generate_schema.py` builds the model's core schema, wrapping it with any `@model_validator(mode='before')` as a `function-before` schema (`core_schema.no_info_before_validator_function` / `with_info_before_validator_function`, via `functional_validators.py`'s `ModelBeforeValidator` decorator machinery in `_decorators.py`). This before-validator schema sits **outside/around** the union/discriminator schema in the validation pipeline.\n4. **Discriminator resolution**: `pydantic/_internal/_discriminated_union.py` (`apply_discriminators` / `_ApplyInferredDiscriminator`) rewrites the union into a `tagged-union` schema keyed on the literal discriminator field, but this rewrite happens once at schema-build time on the **inner** model/union schema \u2014 it has no visibility into what a `mode='before'` validator does to the raw input dict at runtime.\n\n**Root cause**: `model_validator(mode='before')` executes *before* any field/union validation, at the top of the model's core-schema call chain (pydantic-core evaluates `function-before` wrapping the rest of the schema). If that validator does something like reconstructing/filtering the input dict (a common \"pre-processing\" pattern for renaming/normalizing keys) and drops or fails to propagate the discriminator key, the wrapped tagged-union schema then receives a dict lacking the tag. Pydantic-core's tagged-union validator, given no matching discriminator value, falls through however the union was declared (e.g. resolves to whichever variant matches structurally, or a variant where the discriminated field has a default of `None`) \u2014 no `422` is raised because the before-validator didn't error and the union still successfully validates against *some* variant, just not the one the payload was meant for. Because the model still validates cleanly end-to-end, `request_body_to_args()` never appends an error, and FastAPI returns 200 with the field silently `None`.",
